  "key_observations_html": "<aside class=\"crypto-story-callout\" aria-labelledby=\"key-obs-callout-title\"><p class=\"crypto-story-callout__title\" role=\"heading\" aria-level=\"3\" id=\"key-obs-callout-title\">Key observations</p><ul class=\"crypto-story-callout__list\"><li><strong>TMMF distributed value rose 2.5% over 30D:</strong> With distributed value at $13.10B (2.5% higher over 30D), more institutional cash appears to be parking in tokenized MMFs\u2014supporting the view that TMMFs are being used as operational liquidity, not just a niche yield experiment. Related: <a href=\"https://www.theblock.co/news/markets/2026-08-18-securitize-neubergers-230-billion-fixed-income-platform-onchain-new-tokenized-fund-412102\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">Securitize brings Neuberger\u2019s $230 billion fixed-income platform onchain with new tokenized fund</a> (The Block).</li><li><strong>A global regulatory arbitrage map is emerging:</strong> distributed value clusters into distinct compliance regimes\u2014<strong>U.S. Reg D</strong> ~41% of population AUM (e.g. BUIDL, iBENJI); <strong>U.S. Reg S</strong> ~39% of population AUM (e.g. USYC, USDY); <strong>U.S. mutual fund (N-1A)</strong> ~6% of population AUM (e.g. WTGXX). Issuers appear to anchor products in familiar safe harbors rather than one global standard. Related: <a href=\"https://cointelegraph.com/news/neuberger-launches-tokenized-fixed-income-fund-with-securitize?utm_source=rss_feed&amp;utm_medium=rss&amp;utm_campaign=rss_partner_inbound\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">Neuberger teams with Securitize on multi-chain tokenized fixed-income fund launch</a> (CoinTelegraph).</li><li><strong>Issuer models are splitting the TMMF market:</strong> The market is still bifurcating: institutional settlement wrappers concentrate AUM in few holders, while retail-leaning yield products stay more holder-dispersed. Related: <a href=\"https://thedefiant.io/news/tradfi-and-fintech/tempo-earn-embedded-stablecoin-yield-deel\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">Tempo Launches Embedded Yield Product for Platforms, Starting With Deel</a> (The Defiant).</li><li><strong>Rates still matter as much as product and chain choice:</strong> Rate and money-market moves can reshape fund-level inflows as quickly as any chain or product launch story. Related: <a href=\"https://cointelegraph.com/news/interstice-falconx-cross-chain-swap-engine-canton-solana-ethereum-robinhood-chain?utm_source=rss_feed&amp;utm_medium=rss&amp;utm_campaign=rss_partner_inbound\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">FalconX, Interstice Connect Canton to Ethereum, Solana and Robinhood Chain</a> (CoinTelegraph).</li><li><strong>Settlement economics are reshaping network share:</strong> Fee and throughput advantages can pull 30D network-share toward the chains that keep settlement cheaper and more operationally reliable. Related: <a href=\"https://www.coindesk.com/business/2026/08/19/china-triples-digital-yuan-bank-roster-year-to-date-as-eight-more-banks-join-network\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">China triples its e-CNY network in 2026 as 8 more banks join the CBDC push this week</a> (CoinDesk).</li></ul><p class=\"crypto-story-callout__note\">Context only\u2014not investment advice. Observations rank fund-level and network aggregates on this page against recent tokenization and money-market headlines. Bullets combine on-page data with recent industry headlines.</p></aside><p class=\"review-note ko-disclaimer\">Key observations are AI generated and should be reviewed for accuracy.</p>",
